{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/focusmode_bar

    The bar which stands in for Boost Union's navbar while focus mode applies.

    It is in the page wherever focus mode can be switched in place, and the stylesheet shows it only
    under the focus mode body class; the theme_dimensions/focusmode module moves that class and the
    header actions without a reload.

    It keeps the navbar and fixed-top classes deliberately: every offset which stops the
    page sliding under a fixed bar is compiled from Boost's own navbar height, and none of
    those selectors matches on the navbar class itself. So the box, the height, the print
    removal and this theme's signature band all come for free, and only the contents change.

    The colour classes and the Bootstrap colour mode arrive already resolved from the layout
    context, which is what lets a Boost Union flavour recolour the bar with no code here.

    The bar is one row which cannot wrap, and the controls hold no free space of their own: an
    auto margin in the stylesheet pushes them to the end of it.

    The exit label follows the entry button's idiom exactly - a span hidden from view below the
    medium breakpoint and a visually-hidden twin shown only there - so the control has an
    accessible name at every width and never two at once.

    Context variables required for this template (described without braces, because a
    Mustache comment closes at the first pair of closing braces it meets):

    * navbarcolorclasses - the colour classes Boost Union resolved for the navbar (navbar-dark for light type)
    * coursename - the course short name, plain spelling, shown as an overline
    * closeurl - where "Exit focus mode" goes, and where the overline links
    * title - the activity name, the page's h1
    * headeractions - list of objects with an html key: the manual completion button or the status badge,
      on a page that opens focused; empty otherwise, and the module moves them in from the page header
    * expanded - whether the reading column is currently widened
    * widthlabel - the width button's name, the same in both states: aria-pressed carries the state
    * hasmore - whether the overflow menu carries anything at all
    * moreitems - list of objects with url and text keys
    * editswitch - core's rendered edit switch, or the empty string
    * leaveform - true when the page leaves focus mode in place: a form the module intercepts, which
      without JavaScript records the choice and reloads the activity; false on a single activity course
      that switched focus mode on, whose exit is the plain link out of the course
    * actionurl - the theme's focus endpoint, which the leave form posts to
    * sesskey - the session key of the leave form
    * cmid - the course module id of the leave form
    * closelabel - the visible text of the close control
    * closetitle - its tooltip

    Example context (json):
    {
        "navbarcolorclasses": "navbar-dark bg-primary",
        "coursename": "APH-2026",
        "closeurl": "https://example.com/course/view.php?id=2#module-4",
        "title": "Vital signs",
        "headeractions": [
            {"html": "<button class='btn btn-outline-secondary' data-action='toggle-manual-completion'>Mark as done</button>"}
        ],
        "expanded": false,
        "widthlabel": "Wide reading column",
        "hasmore": true,
        "moreitems": [
            {"url": "https://example.com/course/modedit.php?update=4", "text": "Settings"},
            {"url": "https://example.com/report/log/index.php?id=2", "text": "Reports"}
        ],
        "editswitch": "",
        "leaveform": true,
        "actionurl": "https://example.com/theme/dimensions/focus.php",
        "sesskey": "AbC123dEf4",
        "cmid": 4,
        "closelabel": "Exit focus mode",
        "closetitle": "Back to the ordinary page"
    }
}}
<nav class="navbar fixed-top dimensions-focusbar dimensions-focus-only {{navbarcolorclasses}}" aria-label="{{#str}}focusmode_bar, theme_dimensions{{/str}}">
    <div class="dimensions-focusbar-heading">
        <a class="dimensions-focusbar-course d-none d-md-block" href="{{closeurl}}">{{coursename}}</a>
        <h1 class="dimensions-focusbar-title">{{title}}</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="dimensions-focusbar-actions">
        {{! One line on purpose: with no action the slot must hold no text node at all, so :empty hides it. }}
        <div class="dimensions-focusbar-headeractions" data-region="dimensions-focus-headeractions">{{#headeractions}}<div class="dimensions-focusbar-action">{{{html}}}</div>{{/headeractions}}</div>
        <button type="button" class="btn dimensions-focusbar-width d-none d-lg-inline-flex" data-action="dimensions-focus-width" aria-pressed="{{#expanded}}true{{/expanded}}{{^expanded}}false{{/expanded}}" title="{{widthlabel}}">
            <span class="dimensions-focusbar-width-expand{{#expanded}} d-none{{/expanded}}" data-region="dimensions-focus-width-expand">{{#pix}} e/resize, core {{/pix}}</span>
            <span class="dimensions-focusbar-width-contract{{^expanded}} d-none{{/expanded}}" data-region="dimensions-focus-width-contract">{{#pix}} e/merge_cells, core {{/pix}}</span>
            <span class="visually-hidden">{{widthlabel}}</span>
        </button>
        {{#hasmore}}
            <div class="dimensions-focusbar-more dropdown">
                <button type="button" class="btn dimensions-focusbar-morebutton" data-bs-toggle="dropdown" data-bs-auto-close="outside" aria-expanded="false" title="{{#str}}focusmode_more, theme_dimensions{{/str}}">
                    <span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}}focusmode_more, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</span>
                    <i class="icon fa fa-ellipsis-vertical fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                </button>
                <div class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end">
                    {{#moreitems}}
                        <a class="dropdown-item" href="{{url}}">{{text}}</a>
                    {{/moreitems}}
                    {{#editswitch}}
                        <div class="dropdown-item-text dimensions-focusbar-editswitch">{{{editswitch}}}</div>
                    {{/editswitch}}
                </div>
            </div>
        {{/hasmore}}
        {{#leaveform}}
            <form class="dimensions-focusbar-leave" method="post" action="{{actionurl}}">
                <input type="hidden" name="sesskey" value="{{sesskey}}">
                <input type="hidden" name="cmid" value="{{cmid}}">
                <input type="hidden" name="action" value="leave">
                <button type="submit" class="btn dimensions-focusbar-close" data-action="dimensions-focus-leave" title="{{closetitle}}">
                    <i class="icon fa fa-xmark fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <span class="dimensions-focusbar-close-label d-none d-md-inline">{{closelabel}}</span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden d-md-none">{{closelabel}}</span>
                </button>
            </form>
        {{/leaveform}}
        {{^leaveform}}
            <a class="btn dimensions-focusbar-close" href="{{closeurl}}" data-action="dimensions-focus-exit" title="{{closetitle}}">
                <i class="icon fa fa-xmark fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                <span class="dimensions-focusbar-close-label d-none d-md-inline">{{closelabel}}</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden d-md-none">{{closelabel}}</span>
            </a>
        {{/leaveform}}
    </div>
</nav>
